{
    "id": "year7-english-modals-lesson-1-intro",
    "title": "Introduction to Modal Verbs: The Power of Auxiliary Verbs",
    "description": "Discover how modal auxiliary verbs like must, should, can, and might alter sentence meaning by expressing varying levels of certainty, obligation, and permission.",
    "duration": 30,
    "level": "Year 7",
    "slides": [
        {
            "id": "slide-1",
            "title": "The Magic of Modality",
            "subtitle": "How One Word Changes Everything",
            "layout": "hero",
            "components": [
                {
                    "id": "intro-text-1",
                    "type": "heading",
                    "props": {
                        "content": "Welcome to the World of Modal Verbs!",
                        "level": 2,
                        "align": "left"
                    }
                },
                {
                    "id": "intro-paragraph-1",
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "props": {
                        "content": "Imagine telling a friend: 'You **must** clean your room' versus 'You **might** clean your room'. Notice how swapping just one small word completely transforms the tone, expectation, and urgency of your sentence! These helper words are called **modal auxiliary verbs**.",
                        "align": "left"
                    }
                },
                {
                    "id": "warmup-poll-1",
                    "type": "poll",
                    "props": {
                        "question": "Which sentence sounds the most forceful to you?",
